WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.674 --> 00:00:18.039
Sunday morning Nat eagerly ran downstairs, but he started coughing as soon as he greeted Jo.

2
00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:22.341
"No church for you today," Jo said with a frown.

3
00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:25.884
"You should stay home with my sons and me."

4
00:00:28.652 --> 00:00:36.215
"But they're practically babies, and I'm 12 years—" Nat's coughs interrupted his protest.

5
00:00:38.016 --> 00:00:43.798
So Nat spent the morning in Jo's study, learning a hymn and listening to her read aloud.

6
00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:52.422
Jo showed him her "Sunday closet," which was filled with books, art supplies, and building blocks.

7
00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:59.548
"I want everyone to treat Sunday as a day for quiet activities," she explained.

8
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:03.070
"But you can still learn things on Sundays."

9
00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.771
"You mean lessons about how to be good?"

10
00:01:08.192 --> 00:01:12.554
Jo nodded and reached for a thick book, filled with handwritten pages.

11
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:17.816
She flipped to a page with only one word at the top: Nat.

12
00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:19.837
"That's my name!"

13
00:01:20.277 --> 00:01:23.338
he cried, looking both surprised and interested.

14
00:01:23.358 --> 00:01:26.920
"Yes, I have a page for each boy.

15
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.282
I keep track of how he behaves during the week and show it to him on Sunday night.

16
00:01:34.643 --> 00:01:40.846
If the report is bad, I'm disappointed; if it's good, I'm proud," Jo went on.

17
00:01:43.108 --> 00:01:47.070
"No matter what, I hope the boys know I want to help them.

18
00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.832
I also hope they'll try their best because they love Mr.

19
00:01:51.872 --> 00:01:52.533
Bauer and me."

20
00:01:52.553 --> 00:01:55.574
"Oh, I'll try to make you proud!"

21
00:01:57.635 --> 00:01:58.796
Jo hugged Nat.

22
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.184
"I'll be happy if you follow our few rules, get along with the other boys, and learn something."

23
00:02:07.185 --> 00:02:12.069
After lunch Jo took her sons and Daisy into town to visit family.

24
00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:19.193
Everyone else went for a long walk, but Nat wasn't strong enough for that much exercise.

25
00:02:21.255 --> 00:02:24.617
So Tommy offered to show him the gardens and the animals.

26
00:02:26.699 --> 00:02:28.540
First they strolled into the barn.

27
00:02:31.488 --> 00:02:35.912
"We all have pets," Tommy explained, proudly showing off his guinea pig.

28
00:02:35.932 --> 00:02:41.336
"Those white mice are Rob's, and Demi keeps turtles over there."

29
00:02:47.281 --> 00:02:47.922
in this box?"

30
00:02:48.302 --> 00:02:51.945
Nat asked, pointing to a deep box, half-full of dirt.

31
00:02:51.965 --> 00:02:55.028
"That's Jack's worm farm.

32
00:02:56.149 --> 00:02:59.852
He digs up worms and keeps them there until we go fishing so he can sell them to

33
00:02:59.972 --> 00:03:04.574
us. Last time he charged me too much for some little worms.

34
00:03:06.115 --> 00:03:08.636
But that's Jack—he loves money!"

35
00:03:08.656 --> 00:03:11.558
"Who owns the puppies I saw in the house?"

36
00:03:11.978 --> 00:03:12.679
Nat asked.

37
00:03:12.699 --> 00:03:17.001
"The white one is Rob's and the yellow one is Teddy's.

38
00:03:18.542 --> 00:03:20.843
They like to chase Daisy's cat, Topaz."

39
00:03:22.604 --> 00:03:25.306
Nat looked around the barn at all the animals.

40
00:03:25.326 --> 00:03:31.393
"That donkey would be my first choice for a pet," he said, remembering how far he used to

41
00:03:31.453 --> 00:03:32.694
walk with his violin.

42
00:03:34.174 --> 00:03:36.995
Riding a donkey would have saved him lots of time.

43
00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:41.477
"Mr. Laurence gave Toby to Mrs.

44
00:03:41.537 --> 00:03:44.739
Bauer so she and Teddy can ride when we go for walks."

45
00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.900
Nat shook his head in amazement.

46
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.202
"Where do you get all these animals?"

47
00:03:52.222 --> 00:03:57.204
"We find them or buy them, or people give them to us.

48
00:03:58.672 --> 00:03:59.793
My father sent mine.

49
00:04:02.495 --> 00:04:04.456
Here, I'll show you my two chickens."

50
00:04:06.918 --> 00:04:12.361
Nat sighed because he had neither the money to buy a pet nor a father to buy him

51
00:04:12.561 --> 00:04:16.544
one. He followed Tommy into the hayloft.

52
00:04:18.105 --> 00:04:20.607
"I'll tell you what I'll do," Tommy said.

53
00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:23.569
"I hate hunting for eggs.

54
00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.392
If you gather them, I'll give you one egg from every dozen.

55
00:04:29.824 --> 00:04:30.645
I sell them to Mrs.

56
00:04:30.705 --> 00:04:34.027
Bauer, and when you've got a dozen, she'll pay you too."

57
00:04:34.047 --> 00:04:37.389
"Then I can buy whatever I want!"

58
00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.231
Nat said, grinning at the prospect.

59
00:04:42.773 --> 00:04:47.957
He quickly found two eggs, and Tommy generously let him keep one right away.

60
00:04:49.858 --> 00:04:55.262
Then Tommy wrote "Tommy Bangs Company" on the barn wall with a piece of chalk.

61
00:04:55.282 --> 00:05:00.638
"You can keep track of your eggs here," Tommy said, handing Nat the chalk.

62
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:12.167
After that, the boys went outside, where Nat met two horses, six cows, one calf, and three pigs.

63
00:05:14.989 --> 00:05:18.852
Tommy and Nat climbed into a willow tree that hung over a brook.

64
00:05:18.872 --> 00:05:24.837
"You can see our gardens from here," Tommy said.

65
00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:28.320
"Everybody grows a different type of plant."

66
00:05:29.732 --> 00:05:31.393
"Do you think I'll have a garden?"

67
00:05:31.413 --> 00:05:32.554
Nat asked eagerly.

68
00:05:32.574 --> 00:05:34.595
"Of course you will!"

69
00:05:34.895 --> 00:05:36.416
said a friendly voice below.

70
00:05:38.038 --> 00:05:42.781
The boys looked down and saw the professor, who had just returned from his walk.

71
00:05:44.322 --> 00:05:48.705
Nat easily climbed down from the tree, but Tommy fell into the brook!

72
00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:53.808
you okay?"

73
00:05:54.228 --> 00:05:54.989
Nat cried.

74
00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.572
Tommy climbed out of the water with a rueful grin.

75
00:06:01.684 --> 00:06:07.026
"Yeah, that happens all the time," he said and hurried to the house to dry off.

76
00:06:08.487 --> 00:06:09.447
"How are things going?"

77
00:06:09.807 --> 00:06:11.168
the professor asked Nat.

78
00:06:11.188 --> 00:06:14.209
"Are you prepared for school tomorrow?"

79
00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.671
"Well Nat paused.

80
00:06:17.691 --> 00:06:21.732
"I'm worried the boys will laugh when they see how little I know."

81
00:06:21.752 --> 00:06:26.494
"Ah, but you have skills and qualities they lack.

82
00:06:27.955 --> 00:06:30.496
You can play the violin, and you want to learn."

83
00:06:31.988 --> 00:06:34.029
Mr. Bauer patted Nat's shoulder.

84
00:06:34.049 --> 00:06:38.330
"Don't worry—the boys will help you with your lessons."

85
00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.831
And Nat soon found that to be true.

86
00:06:43.171 --> 00:06:49.953
As time passed, he settled in, planting beans in his garden, and earning money by fiddling at neighbors'

87
00:06:50.013 --> 00:07:01.360
picnics. Fritz, he reminds me so much of Beth and her music," Jo whispered one evening as she

88
00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.201
and the professor listened to Nat.

89
00:07:03.221 --> 00:07:08.983
"Yes, Nat's a good boy, although he sometimes tells lies.

90
00:07:10.884 --> 00:07:15.066
Last week he denied stepping on plants in the garden, even though there were witnesses.

91
00:07:16.867 --> 00:07:19.428
And today he lied to me about studying for a test."

92
00:07:21.168 --> 00:07:26.110
"Nat learned from his father that lying is the best way to avoid punishment," Jo said.

93
00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:36.523
"They're mostly small lies," the professor went on, "but nevertheless I'm afraid they'll get him into trouble one

94
00:07:36.543 --> 00:07:36.784
day."
